WEBVTT

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:56.050
Damn it...

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:57.040
Damn...

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.240
My hand...

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:03.850
My hand's...

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.930
Idiot, don't touch it!

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:07.900
Your injury will only get worse if you do.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.640
But, we can't even wrap a bandage around your hand like this.

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:37.310
Snap out of it!

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:39.510
I'll get you to the doctor as soon as I can, okay?

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:55.230
Damn you, you fishbowl bastard!

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.240
"Section I soldiers don't die on the bed."

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:04.560
Yeah, I've been aware of that ever since I joined the section.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:09.200
We were told that our deaths wouldn't be from
a knife stabbing or a shootout or anything pretty like that.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:14.330
Damn it!

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.030
But...

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:26.740
But...

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.770
No one told me I'd die being burnt to death...

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:43.700
Cold...

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:56.770
It's cold...

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:00.120
It's cold...

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:02.840
But...

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:10.930
Burning... warms up... a bit...

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.240
Warms up my heart...

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.000
There are refugees in the sewers?

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.120
Yes.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.210
"We'll get jobs if we go to the capital."

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.490
"We'll be able to manage if we go to the capital."

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:49.530
Many of the people who lost their places because of the war come to this city with those beliefs.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.750
But, the reality is never as friendly as their dreams.

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:57.990
This is the reality.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.690
They have no food or shelter.

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:05.010
They came down to the sewers since they had nowhere to go.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.920
There are a lot of people down here.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:11.830
It's like a whole town by itself.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.670
You're probably right.

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:16.290
The privately-owned waterworks company, Mione Inc.,

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:20.730
has established a sewage network
that runs throughout the entire city.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:24.640
It'd probably be a good estimate to say that...

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:27.340
...there's an equal amount of people living down here as there are people living on the surface.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:29.120
Are you kidding me?

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:32.000
Leave me alone already!

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:36.060
No matter how many times you ask me, I just don't have the money to pay!

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:38.120
Hmph, you illegal residents.

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:39.690
Listen up, sis.

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:45.930
These sewers are the legal property of our waterworks management company.

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:46.720
Okay?!

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:50.820
And you guys came in here and started living here without any permission.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:53.910
You need to at least pay "rent".

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:55.630
B-But...

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:57.770
If you don't have the money...

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:01.420
Then work it off with your body, sis.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:08.350
Just when I thought you were just a little kid,

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:10.800
you seem to have grown up pretty well...

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:18.960
Let's see...

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:20.310
Don't be scared-

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:21.650
Looks really soft...

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:22.870
Eh?!

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:24.490
A soldier?!

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:27.140
Ah, go right ahead.

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:29.820
Hey, you were going to touch her first anyway.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:30.500
Right?

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:33.330
You make it kind of hard for me like that, umm...

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:34.790
WAIT A MINUTE!

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:36.780
Who the hell are you?

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:39.840
Man, you're pretty cute.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:40.750
What's your name?

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.310
Have you been here for a long time?

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:46.370
Hey punk! You think you can just defy us like that?

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.310
Attention!

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:54.050
We are Imperial Army S.S. III, Pumpkin Scissors unit!

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:57.810
We will now bring you out of these sewers.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.150
Pumpkin?

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:06.650
I thought we made a deal with the army already.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.060
Wait.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:11.900
We don't have anywhere to go if we leave this place.

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:13.430
Don't worry.

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:15.660
No one's said this was an eviction.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:19.620
We have established a new state-run farm.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.040
We will ask that you make a living there.

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:24.840
Then, we'd be able to work?

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.300
That's nice of the higher-ups to do.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.780
Like I said, we're "bringing you out".

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:41.630
Hey, Metz.

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:44.000
Can we just let them do that?

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:46.120
Yeah, sure.

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:49.120
But if the boss finds out about this...

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:52.180
Calm down already.

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:55.850
There's no way these refugees would want to walk out of these sewers.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:01.100
Look, speak of the devil.

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:03.690
Why not, Dad?

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:05.580
You'd get a job.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.840
We can live under the sun again.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:11.990
Why...

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:14.920
Why don't you want to leave this place?

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:16.000
LT.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:16.980
What is it?

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:17.950
Well...

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:23.040
Just that some people over there are really stubborn and don't want to leave this place.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:23.960
What?

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:24.900
What are they...

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.900
It'll be all right, so let's go, okay?

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:29.510
What is wrong with them?

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:32.900
Yo, no one asked for soldiers to come down here.

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:37.700
Leave our property already, soldiers.

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:41.790
The era of the soldiers has ended already!

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:46.830
Just get out of here and have your soldier games somewhere no one can see you-

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:49.130
Wh-What's this dog?

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:49.730
Hey, come on, Mercury!
Wh-What's this dog?

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:51.210
Hey, come on, Mercury!

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:53.550
Stop it!

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:56.010
Get off of me, you!

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:06.490
What... what a waste...

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:08.190
Dad?

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:24.540
Doesn't seem like... cold medicine, does it?

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:28.460
You better explain the meaning of this.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:31.670
Hunks!

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:34.550
Explain the meaning of this!

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:36.740
What?

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:38.000
You sure are noisy.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.550
Stop fooling with me!

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:44.170
You sent your men to mess with
the waterworks company, right?!

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:51.140
The sewers?

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:54.000
We're just getting the war refugees out of there.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:58.350
There are plenty of other refugee colonies elsewhere.

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:02.120
Our section was investigating those sewers already.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:03.770
Oh?

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.670
Then...

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:13.200
...Section I knew about this little guy already, huh?

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:19.130
Note: "Himmel" is German for "Heaven"
Himmel investigations aren't Section III's task.

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:24.390
Sure it is; it's a legitimate war relief task.

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:30.600
This thing is an obstacle to war relief.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:34.650
Our section will destroy it.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.870
What happened to the waterworks staff you arrested?

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:50.750
We're diligently questioning him right now.

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:58.970
2nd Lieutenant, please don't be so violent.

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:02.770
Hey, you guys, this is kind of like torture, you know?!

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:05.980
As soldiers, aren't you ashamed?!

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:13.030
People like you who reap money off of people that have lost their hopes for the future and purposes of living on...

00:11:13.030 --> 00:11:14.980
Don't be telling me how soldiers should be!

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:19.070
I'll just say one thing.

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:25.630
Mione Waterworks Company is an important customer of the army that donates a lot of money to us.

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:45.140
Greetings, greetings.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:48.430
It seems one of my men caused some trouble.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:52.240
Waterworks President, Albert Mione here.

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:01.610
Why was he released?!

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:06.560
Because the president of the company came in person to post bail.

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:09.280
Legally, there's no problem.

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:11.620
He was released.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:13.470
That's...

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:16.050
That money...

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:19.340
...is the flesh and blood of the refugees.

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:22.880
Excuse me.

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:26.930
Are you going to invade the waterworks company?

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:34.180
We, Section III, have no jurisdiction to conduct investigations or issue arrest warrants for regular crimes.

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:39.270
...Except when offenders are spotted at the scene...

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:48.740
Imperial S.S. III Pumpkin Scissors...

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:51.690
...will now head to the sewers once again...

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:56.130
...to resume its mission to guide
the refugees to the state-run farm.

00:13:00.660 --> 00:13:02.330
C-Come on...

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:04.860
Sell it to me a bit cheaper...

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:06.190
Hey, hey.

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:08.840
We've got plenty of customers lining up for this.

00:13:12.010 --> 00:13:12.820
Wha-

00:13:14.090 --> 00:13:15.100
You're-

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:17.480
Umm...

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:20.700
With our establishment of the new state-run farm,

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:25.200
we are here to bring refugees out and guide them...

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:26.670
Ahh.

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:27.910
What are you guys doing there?

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:32.040
Sergeant Major, oh no.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:35.170
That must be Himmel.

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:37.990
Hey!

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:39.210
A flagrant criminal offender!

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:43.070
Secure the suspect and the evidence right away!

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:44.960
Yahoo...

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:54.190
Man, you guys should use your heads more.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:55.520
This is useless.

00:13:56.050 --> 00:13:59.440
I'll just get released right away like last time.

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:02.860
Then we'll just arrest you no matter how many times it takes.

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:37.390
Fools!

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:40.200
Our clientele is decreasing.

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:42.820
Unnecessary usage of funds is increasing.

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:45.150
Are you all losers or what?!

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:51.100
Umm, we're really thankful towards you, Boss.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:54.870
You get us released on the same day we get arrested.

00:14:55.070 --> 00:14:56.080
Hmph.

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:58.050
You guys and your big mouths...

00:14:58.050 --> 00:15:00.400
If you guys let my name slip,

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:04.000
the army can come and arrest me right away, you know?!

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:05.100
No way!

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:08.120
There's no way we'd betray you like that, Boss!

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:11.260
You were the only one that took care of bums like us!

00:15:15.090 --> 00:15:20.270
Really, then do me another favor, will you?

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:22.310
Y-Yeah!

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:23.870
Count on us!

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:26.240
We'll... we'll do anything!

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:27.480
Right?

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:36.780
Then, use these to get rid of those annoying flies in the army.

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:40.160
Wow, these aren't crap rifles!

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:42.670
They're brand new babies.

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:45.040
Plenty of ammo, too.

00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:49.400
But where did the boss get these things?

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:53.890
I'm counting on you guys.

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:56.390
Y-Yes, sir!

00:15:57.370 --> 00:15:58.910
All right, let's go!

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:00.130
Yeah!

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:12.860
They're useless now.

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:23.550
Then...

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:38.470
Hey, are you here?

00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:43.210
Hans!

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:46.520
Hans!!!

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:53.060
Are you listening, eh?!

00:16:57.390 --> 00:16:59.730
Time for you to work, okay?!

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:06.640
It's cold...

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:15.070
LT, they're nowhere to be found today.

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:18.780
Maybe they've learned their lesson.

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:20.970
I'd be thankful if that's the case.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:27.060
They're sniping at us!

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:27.810
Get down!

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:31.610
We did it?

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:32.400
Everyone, out!

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:36.630
Fire!

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:37.360
Turn!

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:46.710
Damn it.

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:47.540
They're coming!

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:52.460
Even here?!

00:17:57.140 --> 00:17:58.590
Idiot, don't get up!

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:00.090
What?

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:10.150
Kill!

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:13.610
Kill!

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:15.860
Kill!

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:24.550
Kill!

00:18:38.980 --> 00:18:40.070
Are they coming?

00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:42.350
We've ditched for now.

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:49.070
Your big body does help sometimes.

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:50.680
Right?

00:18:51.550 --> 00:18:53.710
Y-Yo, big guy?

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:55.360
Were you hit somewhere?

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:03.700
N-No... I'm okay...

00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:08.800
Damn it...

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:11.600
I'm part of Section III now!

00:19:14.310 --> 00:19:15.150
LT,

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:16.690
I just noticed.

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:19.630
Those guns they had...

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:21.930
They weren't the old models.

00:19:23.530 --> 00:19:24.700
Indeed.

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:27.470
In fact, they were just like...

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:32.980
Just like... what?

00:19:34.710 --> 00:19:36.460
No, it's nothing.

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:39.620
Let's concentrate on getting out of here.

00:19:44.050 --> 00:19:44.950
Stop the engine!

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.270
Ah, y-yes, sir!

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.660
LT, what's the matter?

00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:54.600
LT!

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:58.530
What's this feeling?

00:19:58.990 --> 00:20:00.550
I've felt this before...

00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:03.030
Are you okay, LT?

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:06.700
That's right, it's him.

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:10.310
It's the same feeling as when I first met him.

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:13.100
LT!

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:16.520
Ahead of us.

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:18.670
Enemy reinforcements?

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:25.290
He's not moving.

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:26.530
What shall we do?

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:27.750
Start the engine.

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:29.040
We don't know what's going on.

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:45.640
Is he... an enemy?

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:55.070
What is that? He's all wrapped up.

00:20:55.070 --> 00:20:57.480
That weapon is a flamethrower.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:58.700
Flame?

00:20:59.830 --> 00:21:00.820
As in, that flame?

00:21:05.940 --> 00:21:08.950
But that project should've been terminated a long time ago.

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:11.450
And why was it terminated?

00:21:12.630 --> 00:21:14.210
They realized...

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:20.210
...that it became a weapon that allowed humans to kill others in a way they shouldn't be.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:29.510
Afterwards, all manner of killings that go against humane principles were supposed to be forbidden in the Empire...

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:32.140
He's coming for us.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:34.090
It's cold...

00:21:37.470 --> 00:21:38.690
It's cold...

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:45.130
Wh-What shall we do?

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:46.000
He's coming.

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:51.330
It's cold...

00:21:52.030 --> 00:21:55.880
So... I'm going to burn you guys...

00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:34.180
Mer-kun, the corporal looks kind of weird!

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:36.390
Oreld is about to do something perverted, too!

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:38.630
What's going to happen to Section III?!

00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:41.520
Next time, "Astray Decisions".

00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:43.380
Come get us if you're not scared!
